FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block D   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Rosemary Tambouret MD Signed On  06 MAY 04 at 16 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue with a short suture denoting the superior and a long suture the lateral margin  The superior margin is marked with blue ink  the inferior margin with black ink  the medial margin with green ink and the lateral margin with yellow ink  The specimen is serially sectioned from the anterior to the posterior aspect to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm  ill defined  tan lesion with irregular borders which extends to 0 3cm of the superior margin  0 4cm of the medial margin  0 8cm to the lateral margin  1 3cm to the inferior margin  1 7cm to the inferior margin and greater than 2 5cm from the posterior margin  The remainder of the tissue consists predominantly of adipose tissue with a scant amount of intervening soft  white fibrous tissue  There are a few cysts identified in the fibrous tissue which measure up to 0 4cm in diameter  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Anterior margin  B E  Lesion identified on specimen radiograph  F  Fibrous tissue with cyst  G  Posterior margin  Please note that the wire is received detached from the specimen and there is a 0 5cm linear tract identified in the lesion  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node hot and blue   REMOVED_CASE_ID  and   REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fibrofatty tan yellow soft tissue  The specimen is trisected and entirely submitted in cassettes H I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional posterior tissue medial margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan yellow focally cauterized soft tissue which is bivalved and entirely submitted in cassettes J K  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved superior 1 2  are 2 tan yellow focally hemorrhagic and cauterized soft tissue fragments aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The specimen is trisected and entirely submitted in cassettes L N  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved inferior 1 2  is a tan yellow focally cauterized and hemorrhagic unoriented soft tissue specimen  The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The specimen is bivalved and entirely submitted in cassettes O P  Gross Description by  TIM J  ROBINSON Resident  ANDRAS SCHAFFER  MD PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE RIGHT SENTINEL   REMOVED_CASE_ID      REMOVED_CASE_ID   EXCISION PART C  BREAST RIGHT POSTERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN  EXCISION PART D  BREAST RIGHT FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN  EXCISION PART E  BREAST RIGHT FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN  EXCISION , No.
