Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 MAY 97 ACCESSIONED ON  07 MAY 97 at 08 48 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM AS MEASURED ON A GLASS SLIDE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  WITH A FOCUS OF LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   Note  The invasive carcinoma has features similiar to that of invasive micropapillary carcinoma which is described by Siriaunkgul and Tavassoli  Modern Pathology  Vol 6  No 6  REMOVED_DATE Dr  Koerner has reviewed select slides and agrees with the above interpretation  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The tumor cells do not stain immunohistochemically for S 100  smooth muscle actin  or chromogranin  Rare tumor cells stain for Grimelius  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 97 at 18 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 MAY 97 at 15 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen SEction Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of breast tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pink  firm  irregular mass with an eccentric round hemorrhagic area extending to the inked margin  Entirely submitted in A through J  with nodule in G through J  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST NODULE  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 25 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  100    MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE 2 3 3   PRESENT AT INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The carcinoma measures approximately 1 7cm in greatest dimeter  No definitive vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm fibrofatty tissue fragment  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  white firm  well demarcated nodule grossly abutting the inked margin  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder are submitted entirely in A through I  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , No.
