Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 49 CLINICAL DATA  Previous ductal cell cancer right breast in  REMOVED_CASE_ID                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  ABOUT 70   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  ABOUT 30    SEE NOTE  NOTE  Tumor focally invades the deep dermis of the overlying skin  Tumor is focally present within a few cell diameters of the inked margin  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 58                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE  6   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor specimen consists  predominantly of an in situ disease  The 6  relects invasive tumor only  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 16     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 132 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Not determined Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Si