sitive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are five parts  Labeled  Re excision breast cancer  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm  tan pink and yellow  soft tissue mass with a 4 x 0 7cm skin ellipse running longitudinally  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a mottled tan and yellow cut surface  with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm hemorrhagic cyst near one pole of the specimen  Representative sections through the specimen are submitted in cassettes A through F  with cyst containing sections in cassettes A through C  Labeled  Superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  yellow white  soft tissue fragment  submitted entirely in cassette G  Labeled  Inferior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  yellow  soft tissue fragment  submitted entirely in cassette H  Labeled  Medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  tan  soft tissue fragment  submitted entirely in cassette I  Labeled  Lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan and brown  soft tissue fragment  submitted entirely in cassette J  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  RIGHT  PART B 