Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  19 AUG 97 at 17 22 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma on recent core biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    REMOVED_DATE CM  GREATEST GROSS DIMENSION OF A STELLATE TUMOR   GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE CLOSEST  DEEP  MARGIN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    LOW GRADE  SOLID TYPE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  MICROCALCIFICATIONS WITHIN BENIGN BREAST TISSUE  NOTE  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT  DEEP INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 14 OR 14 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  21 AUG 97 at 21 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labelled with the patients name  unit number and   Right breast lump   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE X 3 0cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen was inked superior margin black  deep margin black  inferior margin blue  lateral margin red  medial margin yellow  anterior margin green  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm well defined stellate tan to white firm mass  coming within 0 2cm of the closest inferior margin  Section through the tumor including the closest inferior margin are submitted from medial to lateral in cassette A  B and C  Representative section away from the tumor are submitted in cassettes D and E  Received fresh  labelled with the patients name  unit number and  Right breast deep inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm soft  yellow white piece of breast with a suture marking the margin farthest from the tumor  The furthest margin is inked black  the opposite side of the specimen is inked green  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette F   I  Received fresh  labelled with the patients name  unit number and  Right axillary content  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm soft  white yellow piece of adipose tissue  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes J   M  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION  TUMOR CLOSE TO INTERNAL DEEP MARGIN  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                 