tion  Sectioning through the breast parenchyma demonstrates a firm  fibrotic region deep within the parenchyma of the breast which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm  This tissue is white and rubbery and has an appearance of fibrosis  It focally extends to within 0 2cm to the deep margin  The remaining breast tissue consists of lobules of adipose tissue with interspersed streaks of white  fibrous tissue  The previous biopsy cavity beneath the transverse central scar is not grossly evident at this time  SECTION CODE  A D  breast tissue under the central transverse scar  E F  representative sections from the medial one half of the breast  G  representative section from the central portion of the breast including inferior margin  H I  representative sections from the lateral half of the breast including tissue from underneath the vertical scar described  J  possible lymph nodes from the edge of the right upper outer quadrant  K  nipple  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of nodular  fibrofatty breast tissue  After inking  sectioning reveals white  curly  gray  fibrous tissue and a scant amount of fat  No areas suspicious for invasive carcinoma are identified  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes L through Q  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST TISSUE   NO LESIONS GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PART B  BREAST  BIOPSY  LEFT    report_end  , No.
