nd beyond the region of the invasive carcinoma  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ comes to  0 1cm from the medial  inferior  and posterior margins  That some of these foci interpreted as in situ carcinoma may actually represent bluntly invasive carcinoma cannot be entirely excluded  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  left breast biopsy with needle loc   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  tan yellow to focally hemorrhagic portion of irregular fibroadipose tissue with a short suture designating superior  a long suture designating lateral  and a needle localization wire in place  The specimen is inked according to protocol  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green  inferior   yellow  and serially sectioned from medial to lateral  Sectioning reveals a lobulated  tan yellow cut surface with focal hemorrhagic areas  No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  The specimen is submitted entirely as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial en face margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Body of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral en face margin  The area of possible calcifications is in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assesse