d with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 93 at 15 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left beast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of white  tan to red  fibro fatty breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a yellow to white and firm parenchyma  There are no discrete masses present  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  Tissue taken for BRDU  Remaining specimen submitted in toto as A through N  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , No.
