y a radiograph  The specimen is oriented per the surgeon as follows  Short stitch   superior  long stitch   lateral  The long axis of the specimen is the superior inferior axis  and the specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  medial   green  lateral   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal cut surfaces predominantly with gray tan  fibrous tissue with focal grittiness at the inferior aspect of the specimen  The specimen is submitted in toto from inferior to superior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the inferior margin en face in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the superior margin en face in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   Breast  Right   Excision  report_end  , No.
