 o clock scar  a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm is identified  with firm fibrous tissue around it  The biopsy cavity is 0 1cm from the closest margin  which is the deep margin  The subareolar biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  and is 5 0cm from the other biopsy cavity and is far away from all margins  On further sectioning a firm area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm with a rubbery yellow white cut surface is seen  at REMOVED_DATE o clock  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code  A D  Biopsy cavity  larger  at 5 o clock  plus closest deep  black inked margin  E  Closest deep margin to subareolar biopsy cavity  F J  Subareolar biopsy cavity  K  Large rubbery fibrotic area at REMOVED_DATE o clock and closest deep margin  L  Frozen Section  1 M  Frozen Section  2 Resident  SHABIN NANJI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 AND  2  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  Mari Mino  MD O R  Diagnosis by  GREGORY LAUWERS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , No.
