Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 MAY 97 ACCESSIONED ON  20 MAY 97 at 13 18 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   REEXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR INFERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 19 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The metastatic carcinoma spans less than 0 2cm and does not transgress the lymph node capsule  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 MAY 97 at 16 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN    THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 MAY 97 at 15 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number in multiple parts  Labeled  re excision  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm skin ellipse with an underlying REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast parenchyma with a short stitch designating superior  a long stitch designating lateral  The specimen is inked with the long lateral margin inked green  short or superior margin black  inferior margin black  anterior margin blue  posterior margin red  medial margin yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity 1 5cm beneath the skin ellipse  Contains surrounding ill defined firm  bright yellow and tan to yellow tissue  but without any definite nodules or masses  Areas of firm  bright yellow tissue abut the green and blue margins  anterior lateral margin   The remainder of the breast reveals areas of ill defined white to tan firm tissue  Section code  A D  biopsy cavity E H  representative sections of abnormal surrounding tissue I  long or lateral margin with abnormal tissue Labeled  additional anterior inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue inked and entirely submitted in J  Labeled  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue sectioned to reveal multiple pink tan lymph nodes  the largest measuring 1 0cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections in K 0  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL