Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 37 CLINICAL DATA  FNA phylloids tumor  also calcification on mammography                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST   RIGHT BREAST WITH NEEDLE LOCALIZATION    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  WITH ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  INVOLVING NODULAR SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  No definite stromal  blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Architectural distortion secondary to the prominent sclerosing adenosis makes assessment of stromal invasion difficult  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH PROMINENT SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  B  BREAST   RIGHT BREAST NODULE   EXCISION   PHYLLOIDES TUMOR  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  FOCALLY INFARCTED WITH INCREASED MITOTIC ACTIVITY  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR MARGIN   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor does not display infiltrative borders  marked increased stromal cellularity nor marked cellular pleomorphism  Focally  Slide O   the tumor displays 6 mitotic figures per 10 high power fields  Based on the increased mitotic activity and focal infarction this tumor is best classified as intermediate grade  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 05                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast with needle localization  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm piece of fibroadipose tissue inked and sectioned to reveal a  7cm tan white  firm area that extends to less than 0 1cm of an inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and resubmitted in cassette A  The remaining nodule is in cassette B and the rest of the specimen is in cassettes C through F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast nodule  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm fragment of firm  rubbery breast tissue a long stitch marking the lateral margin and a short stitch marking the superior margin  The posterior surface of the specimen is inked yellow on black  The superior surface orange on black and the inferior surface red on black  The anterior  medial  and lateral surfaces are inked black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal pink tan  rubbery cut surface with focal cystic changes  Further sectioning of specimen reveals a firm  rubbery  white tan  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  5cm nodule with white tan nodular cut surface which is present away from the white fibrous tissue in fat in the anterior aspect of the specimen and grossly abuts the anterior resection margin  SECTION CODE G  Lateral resection margin  en face section  H  Representative section of firm  white  rubbery tissue with adjacent superior and posterior resection margin  I  Representative section of firm  white  rubbery tissue with adjacent posterior and inferior resection margin  J  Representative section of firm  white  rubbery tissue with adjacent anterior resection margin  K L  Representative section of separate nodule in anterior fat  M Q  Additional representative section of specimen showing focally white  firm solid and focally cystic cut surface  R  Medial resection margin  en face section  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   BIOPSY  FIBROADENOMA WITH FOCAL DCIS  O R  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCIS