Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 10 32 CLINICAL DATA  79 year old female with abnormal mammogram  calcifications right breast  History right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE  1  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Scattered small microscopic foci involving 6 of 10 blocks and spanning at least 1 1cm  Grade  3  Calcifications  Limited to the carcinoma in situ  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 2cm from the anterior  posterior  and superior margins of the specimen along a broad front  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15 46                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast biopsy with needle localization  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular portion of tan yellow to pink fibrofatty tissue with a localizing needle wire in place  The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph  There is a short stitch designating the superior aspect and long stitch designating the lateral aspect  The interior aspect is inked blue  the posterior aspect is inked black  the superior aspect is inked orange and the inferior aspect is inked yellow  The specimen is sequentially sectioned from the lateral to medial aspect  The cut surface shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm well circumscribed grey white  homogenous rubbery oval mass which abuts the anterior margin and comes to within 0 1cm from the posterior margin  0 3cm from the inferior and 1 2cm from the superior margin  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is predominately dense white fibrous tissue with a minimum amount of tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  There is a 0 2cm cyst located at the medial aspect which is filled with dark brown cloudy fluid  No additional discrete masses or lesions are identified  The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from the lateral to medial aspect in cassettes A J with the well circumscribed mass in cassette D E and the area denoted by the needle localization wire in cassette D G  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , No.
