Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 10 37 CLINICAL DATA  59 year old female with left breast carcinoma diagnosis invasive lobular                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The carcinoma cells do not transgress the lymph node capsule  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   MASTECTOMY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 7 OF 7 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 06 25                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR KERATIN LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  The lymph node contains keratin positive carcinoma cells  three keratin stained sections examined   LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   MASTECTOMY  The lymph nodes do not contain keratin positive carcinoma cells  four keratin stained sections examined   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 06 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan red  rubbery lymph node which is entirely frozen as FX  1 now as A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast and axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast with REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm of attached axillary tail  The breast is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 4 3cm tan skin ellipse which has an eccentric 1 3cm nipple  Located 5 5cm lateral to the nipple is a 2 5cm well healed linear scar  Contiguous with the scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hemorrhagic cavity with adjacent fat necrosis which communicates with the black inked deep margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan white focally gritty dense white fibrous tissue area which communicates with the biopsy cavity    residual tumor   The remaining parenchyma is 85  dense white fibrous to 15  yellow lobulated fatty tissue  Underlying the axillary tail is minimal tan brown muscle  There are multiple tan red rubbery to tan white firm lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in greatest dimension within the axillary tail  Representative sections are submitted as follows  B F  Biopsy cavity to deep  G  Biopsy cavity to deep with   residual tumor  H  Fibrous tissue away from biopsy cavity  I  4 whole lymph nodes  J  4 whole lymph nodes  K L  1 serially sectioned lymph node  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  FCK      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL NODE  1   LYMPH NODE WITH FOCUS  HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  TAI YUAN LIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  William C  Faquin MD PhD O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  1   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY , Yes.
