hemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in two parts and accompanied by radiographs  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma and fatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted in A through J   and U   DD  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm white firm area  1 0cm from the closest margin  The firm area are submitted in K through L  Representative sections from the remainder in M through T  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX  LEFT BREAST   NO AREAS GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  GROSS DX   RIGHT BREAST   SUSPICIOUS AREA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Niels