sitive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast with needle  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm yellow fibroadipose tissue with a suture marking the deep margin and a localizing wire noted by the surgeon to be the anterior lateral point of the specimen  The resection margins are inked as follows  Inferior   blue  superior   black  deep   red  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregularly shaped firm white mass with stellate extension that comes to within 0 2cm from the inferior and the superior resection margin  Representative sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes A through D  C and D are from the same slice divided in the middle   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Superior margin  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unoriented yellow fibroadipose tissue fragment  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable yellow fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes E  F  and G  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm unoriented yellow fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes H through J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s na