en we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 97 at 17 03     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibroadipose tissue fragment with a suture designating the biopsy cavity margin  The margin is inked black and the remainder of the specimen is inked blue  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm hard  tan pink  well circumscribed mass  0 4cm from the biopsy cavity margin and 0 9cm from the other resection margin  The remainder of the specimen is unremarkable  Section code  AandB mass and closest margin CandD uninvolved breast tissue  representative sections Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fibroadipose tissue fragment with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm skin ellipse  The cut surface reveals fibrocystic changes with no grossly evident mass  Section code  E K  breast tissue with radiographic evidence of microcalcification  representative sections L Z  breast parenchyma  representative sections Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST TISSUE  RESECTION MARGIN FREE OF TUMOR  FROZEN SECTION GROSS DIAGNOSIS  2  RIGHT BREAST  NO IDENTIFIABLE TUMOR SEEN  O R  Resident  Navneet Narula  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SPECIMEN  1 PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SPECIMEN  2   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 08 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  INVASIVE  0 5cm  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO AN INKED SURFACE  SEE NOTE   2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCYSTS  INTRALOBULAR FIBROSIS  AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  3  MONCKEBERGS MEDIAL CALCIFIC SCLEROSIS  NOTE  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  carcinoma in situ is not present  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 51                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 12 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fibrofatty fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm nodule  No frozen section done  The fragment is submitted entirely as follows  SECTION CODE  AandB  nodule CandD  regions flanking the nodule E M  unremarkable tissue  Enclosed is the lesions radiograph  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  SUSPICIOUS NODULE  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  SAVED FOR PERMANENT SECTION  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , No.
